# CODEOWNERS — protect privileged CI paths (Issue #361).
#
# Files under these paths run with the repository's secrets and (for
# deploy.yml) an OIDC id-token, so a change to them is high-impact: it could
# exfiltrate secrets (ACTIONS_PUSH, CODECOV_TOKEN, SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN,
# GITLEAKS_LICENSE), push to the default branch, or publish content to the
# public GitHub Pages site. Requiring a trusted owner's review on these
# paths is defence-in-depth on top of the generic single-review rule.
#
# Enforced at merge time by `require_code_owner_review: true` in
# .github/rulesets/develop.json (a repo admin must re-apply that ruleset).
# The @stSoftwareAU/developers team mirrors the required reviewer already
# named in the ruleset.

# Workflow definitions — run with secrets and id-token.
/.github/workflows/   @stSoftwareAU/developers

# Composite/local actions invoked by the privileged workflows.
/.github/actions/     @stSoftwareAU/developers

# Settings-as-code branch-protection ruleset — the controls themselves.
/.github/rulesets/    @stSoftwareAU/developers
